<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ekiti people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ekiti are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> subgroup of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, living in hilly country now forming Ekiti State. Organised in many small kingdoms, they were dominated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibadan">Ibadan</a> from the mid-19th century. In 1877 they formed the Ekitiparapo alliance with the Ijesha and fought Ibadan in the long Kiriji War, ended by British mediation in 1886.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ekiti-people.jpg" alt="Ekiti people" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oramfe · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Ekiti_speaking_Yoruba_people.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
